        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The described plant Gösgen started commercial operation at the end of 1979. It belongs to the 1000 MW class. It has a Siemens designed primary circuit with three loop cooling, a spherical containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for German pressure water reactors of the same class.\n\n# Included processes\nThe module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
